==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɑɣu/|lang=ang}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{proto|Germanic|laguz|water, sea|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|lakw-|lake, pond|lang=ang}}. Cognate with {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|lacus||hollow, pond|lang=la}}, {{etyl|sga|-}} {{term|loch||lake, pond|lang=sga}}, {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|λάκκος||tr=lákkos|waterhole, pond, pit|lang=grc}}.

====Alternative forms====
